# fixedbugs, defect 2335, 2026-11-08: a record of the program's own with one
# field `a`, built `R(a: 1, a: 2)`, was told it is built with every field,
# named `a:`, all of them, always: false, since the construction names `a`
# and misses nothing, while a group's record given a field twice was told
# that, at the second label. A construction giving another count of values
# than its fields was told that rule alone (`check/walk.hero`). Now each
# label at fault is told as a group's is (`check/group_fields.hero`'s
# `short`), and the rule only where a field goes unnamed.
record R
    a: i64

function main()
    r = R(a: 1, a: 2)  #~ wrong_label
    print(r.a)
